course: dictionary
lesson: 6916
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. Read the words around it. «Ten paces to the treasure» means ten steps, because paces here counts steps. «He paced the room» means he walked up and down, often because he was worried.
explain: Pace can also mean speed. «Everyone grows at their own pace» means each person grows at their own speed. «Slacken pace» means slow down, and «at a smart pace» means quickly. To pace yourself is to go at a speed you can keep up, like a runner in a long race.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If "walked up and down" fits «he paced the room» and "speed" does not, you have chosen correctly. If the clues still do not settle it, check a dictionary.
fact: A pace is one step, or the length of one step.
fact: Pace can mean how fast someone moves or how fast something happens.
fact: «Hearken» means listen, and «grave» means serious and worried in old stories.
fact: Walking the same line again and again is called pacing. A bored cat may do it, so good zoos give animals puzzles and new enclosures to reduce it.
fact: «Working at his own pace» means working at his own speed.
exercise: «Ten paces to the treasure.» What does paces mean here? | *Steps | Speeds | Walks up and down | Treasures
exercise: «He paced the room while he waited for the news.» What is he doing? | Sleeping | Singing loudly | Dancing happily | *Walking up and down, worried
exercise: «The runner kept pace with her friends.» What does kept pace mean? | Fell far behind them | Ran in the opposite direction | *Stayed at the same speed as them | Gave them a present
test: «She ran at a smart pace to catch the bus.» What does at a smart pace mean? | *Quickly | Backwards | Very quietly | Slowly
test: To pace yourself means to | Run faster than everyone else | Stop running at once | *Go at a speed you can keep up | Count every step out loud
exam: Jayden says pace only means steps. «Everyone grows at their own pace.» What does pace mean here? | A type of pet | Ten steps long | *The speed at which a person grows | Being worried
